    "content": "Somalia's National Security Advisor, Ambassador Aweys Haji Yusuf Ahmed, stated at the Global Security Forum 2026 in Doha, Qatar, that the Somali government has regained control of more than 55% of the territory formerly held by the militant group al-Shabaab. He also said that at least 1.5 million people have been liberated from the group's intimidation. The remarks were delivered in a speech on 21 October 2026, during a panel on security progress in Somalia.\n\nThe announcement comes amid a sustained military campaign by Somali forces, supported by international partners, to weaken al-Shabaab's grip on rural and urban areas. In recent years, the government has intensified operations in regions such as Hirshabelle and Galmudug, aiming to dislodge the group from key strongholds. The Doha forum provided a platform for Somali officials to present their security achievements to an international audience.\n\nAweys highlighted the collaboration between Somali security forces and local communities, which has been crucial in reclaiming territory. He noted that the liberation of 1.5 million people from al-Shabaab's control marks a significant step toward restoring normal life and governance in affected areas. The advisor also emphasized the importance of continued international support to sustain these gains.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these developments are closely watched, as many have families in the liberated regions and have long contributed to peacebuilding efforts through remittances and advocacy. The diaspora's role in supporting stabilization and reconstruction remains vital, and the reported progress could encourage further investment in Somalia's recovery. However, some community members may remain cautious, given the persistent threat of asymmetric attacks.\n\nThe Somali government's claims reflect its ongoing commitment to defeating al-Shabaab and securing the country. While the figures have not been independently verified, they represent a morale boost for Somali forces and their allies. The international community has repeatedly called for continued support to consolidate security gains and address humanitarian needs in recovered areas.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/10/22/soomaaliya-oo-sheegtay-in-55-dhulkii-as-dib-loo-qabsaday/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=soomaaliya-oo-sheegtay-in-55-dhulkii-as-dib-loo-qabsaday",
